# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked
# into the image. Two entries below are not tidiness, they are the point:
#
#   .env   holds OPENAI_API_KEY and the Supabase *service-role* key, which
#          bypasses row-level security entirely. Secrets belong in the host's
#          environment settings, never in a layer that can be pushed, pulled,
#          cached or shared.
#   venv/  is a Windows CPython 3.12 environment. Copying it into a Linux
#          python:3.11-slim image adds hundreds of megabytes of binaries that
#          cannot run there, and can shadow the packages pip just installed.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local virtualenvs
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local uploads — documents live in Supabase Storage now, and anything sitting
# in this folder is leftover test data from before that change.
uploads/

# Tooling and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
